# Verify after a build

When a build in this chat is finished — a branch, a pull request, or a spec — hand it to the verification agent before you tell the user the build is done.

- Pass the spec path or the claims, and the branch or pull request.
- Wait for the verification agent's report.
- Give that report to the user unchanged.
- If no spec was named, still hand off. The verification agent asks for the spec and stops.

The verification agent is the approver. The work is accepted only when its verdict is pass. Do not call the build done on tests, a clean tree, or a hypothesis. Trust what the drive saw. A failed claim stays failed.

On a fail, the verification agent opens one follow-up in plan mode with the failed claims. That follow-up switches to agent mode and fixes them. Do not open a second follow-up. Do not fix the failures yourself before the report is back. Do not accept the work while the verdict is fail.
